{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/grafluentcollections"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"GrafluentCollections"}],"title":"GrafluentCollections","externalID":"GrafluentCollections","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"],"anchor":"Guides"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import GrafluentCollections"},{"type":"text","text":" imports every module. Each module also has its own documentation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and can be imported on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import GrafluentCollections","","var scores: FenwickTree = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]","print(scores.prefixSum(through: 3))  \/\/ 9","print(scores.sum(in: 2 ..< 6))       \/\/ 19"]},{"anchor":"Values-not-references","type":"heading","text":"Values, not references","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every collection is a copy-on-write struct. Assigning one copies nothing until one of the copies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is mutated; then only that copy pays, once, and the other keeps its elements:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let original: BTree = [1, 2, 3]","var copy = original","copy.insert(4)","Array(original)   \/\/ [1, 2, 3]","Array(copy)       \/\/ [1, 2, 3, 4]"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices of a tree live in flat arrays linked by integer indices rather than in a class per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, so a copy is a few array copies and a traversal reads memory almost in order. The API","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"follows the standard library and Swift Collections: the sorted sets are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SetAlgebra"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"random-access collections indexed by rank, the dictionaries take ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subscript(_:default:)"},{"text":", and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range trees are collections of their values.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Traps-and-checked-spellings","type":"heading","text":"Traps and checked spellings","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A plain spelling traps when its precondition fails, like an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" subscript out of range: it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the fast path, for callers who know the precondition holds. Beside it, a ","type":"text"},{"code":"checked:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" spelling","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws a typed error instead, one of those in ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/CollectionErrors\/documentation\/CollectionErrors","type":"text"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"try?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" turns it into an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let primes: AVLTree = [2, 3, 5, 7]","primes[2]                    \/\/ 5","try primes[checked: 9]       \/\/ throws IndexOutOfRange"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A mutation that would break a structure’s invariant, such as joining two treaps whose elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interleave, throws on its plain spelling and changes nothing. Where the standard library’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collections return an optional (","type":"text"},{"code":"remove(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a dictionary’s subscript, ","type":"text"},{"code":"min()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), these do too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Grafluent-conversions","type":"heading","text":"Grafluent conversions","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A collection whose shape is a tree converts to the Grafluent type of that shape: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"text":", with an initializer on the Grafluent type that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"costs O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":") once. Structures whose shape is a general graph, such as decision diagrams and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automata, offer a view that is a Grafluent graph without copying. Either way, Grafluent’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms, drawings and file formats run over the collection; its own operations never go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through the conversion. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"},{"text":" shows the round trip.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Modules","type":"heading","text":"Modules","level":3},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Group","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Modules"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Search trees","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees"},{"type":"text","text":" (AVL, red–black and splay trees, treaps), "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/BTrees\/documentation\/BTrees"},{"type":"text","text":" (B-trees), "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/SkipLists\/documentation\/SkipLists"},{"type":"text","text":" (skip lists)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tries","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"},{"type":"text","text":" (tries over any sequence of symbols, radix and Patricia trees, Aho–Corasick automata)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Suffix structures","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures","type":"text"},{"text":" (suffix arrays with LCP, suffix trees, suffix automata)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decision diagrams"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams"},{"type":"text","text":" (reduced ordered BDDs, zero-suppressed ZDDs)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Range and spatial trees"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees","type":"text"},{"text":" (Fenwick trees, segment trees with lazy propagation, interval trees), ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees","type":"text"},{"text":" (k-d trees, quadtrees, octrees)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sequences and persistence"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/Ropes\/documentation\/Ropes"},{"type":"text","text":" (ropes: sequences as balanced trees of chunks), "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/PersistentTrees\/documentation\/PersistentTrees"},{"type":"text","text":" (path-copying weight-balanced trees that keep every version)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Caches","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/Caches\/documentation\/Caches"},{"type":"text","text":" (LRU caches)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shared"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/CollectionErrors\/documentation\/CollectionErrors"},{"type":"text","text":": the errors the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked:"},{"type":"text","text":" spellings throw, re-exported by every module that throws them"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Grafluent."}],"references":{"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections","role":"collection","title":"GrafluentCollections","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections","abstract":[{"text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Grafluent.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/ChoosingASearchTree":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree","type":"topic","title":"Choosing a search tree","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/choosingasearchtree","abstract":[{"text":"Pick a sorted set or sorted dictionary by the workload it will see.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/DecisionDiagrams":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","role":"article","title":"Decision diagrams","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/decisiondiagrams","abstract":[{"text":"Represent Boolean functions and families of sets as shared, canonical graphs.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph","type":"topic","title":"Seeing a collection as a graph","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/seeingacollectionasagraph","abstract":[{"text":"Convert a collection’s shape to a Grafluent graph, then lay it out, write it or run an algorithm","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/TriesAndSuffixStructures":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","type":"topic","title":"Tries and suffix structures","url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/triesandsuffixstructures","abstract":[{"text":"Search a set of keys by prefix, or a text by substring.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://GrafluentCollections/documentation/GrafluentCollections/RangeAndSpatialTrees":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","type":"topic","title":"Range and spatial trees","abstract":[{"text":"Answer queries over ranges of a sequence, over intervals, and over points in space.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/grafluentcollections\/rangeandspatialtrees","kind":"article","role":"article"}}}